Doenet-Sync-Version: 0.7.28
Doenet-Sync-NumVariants: 1
Doenet-Sync-Hash: a266e767b9607117
-->
<problem>
<!-- <title>extrema of log(even quartic)</title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="a" from="1" to=" 4" />
<selectFromSequence name="b" from="2" to=" 3" />
<select name="dint1">
  <option><number>-1</number><number>1</number><number>1</number></option>
  <option><number>-1</number><number>2</number><number>1</number></option>
  <option><number>-1</number><number>3</number><number>1</number></option>
  <option><number>1</number><number>-1</number><number>3</number></option>
  <option><number>2</number><number>-1</number><number>3</number></option>
  <option><number>3</number><number>-1</number><number>3</number></option>
</select>
<selectFromSequence name="c" from="1" to=" 10" />
<selectFromSequence name="d" from="-10" to=" 10" exclude="d" />


<function name="quartic" variables="x" symbolic="true"><math expand="true" simplify="numbers">($a *(x^2-$b ^2)^2+$c )</math></function>

<derivative name="dquartic" variables="x">$quartic</derivative>
<function name="fun" variables="x">$d *ln($$quartic(x))</function>
<derivative name="fun_prime" variables="x">$fun</derivative>
<math name="critical_points">-$b,0,$b</math>
<number name="cp1">-$b</number>
<number name="cp2">0</number>
<number name="cp3">$b</number>
<number name="auxpoint1">floor($cp1 -1)</number>
<number name="auxpoint2">($cp1 +$cp2 )/2</number>
<number name="auxpoint3">($cp2 +$cp3 )/2</number>
<number name="auxpoint4">ceil($cp3 +1)</number>
<evaluate function="$fun_prime" input="$auxpoint1" name="fun_prime_a1" />
<evaluate function="$fun_prime" input="$auxpoint2" name="fun_prime_a2" />
<evaluate function="$fun_prime" input="$auxpoint3" name="fun_prime_a3" />
<evaluate function="$fun_prime" input="$auxpoint4" name="fun_prime_a4" />
<conditionalContent name="increasedecrease1">
  <case condition="$fun_prime_a1 >0">
    <text>increasing</text>
  </case>
  <else><text>decreasing</text></else>
</conditionalContent>
<conditionalContent name="increasedecrease2">
  <case condition="$fun_prime_a2 >0">
    <text>increasing</text>
  </case>
  <else><text>decreasing</text></else>
</conditionalContent>
<conditionalContent name="increasedecrease3">
  <case condition="$fun_prime_a3 >0">
    <text>increasing</text>
  </case>
  <else><text>decreasing</text></else>
</conditionalContent>
<conditionalContent name="increasedecrease4">
  <case condition="$fun_prime_a4 >0">
    <text>increasing</text>
  </case>
  <else><text>decreasing</text></else>
</conditionalContent>
<conditionalContent name="cp1_characterization">
  <case condition="$fun_prime_a1 > 0 and $fun_prime_a2 &lt; 0">
    <text>maximum</text>
  </case>
  <case condition="$fun_prime_a1 &lt; 0 and $fun_prime_a2 > 0">
    <text>minimum</text>
  </case>
  <else><text>none</text></else>
</conditionalContent>
<conditionalContent name="cp2_characterization">
  <case condition="$fun_prime_a2 > 0 and $fun_prime_a3 &lt; 0">
    <text>maximum</text>
  </case>
  <case condition="$fun_prime_a2 &lt; 0 and $fun_prime_a3 > 0">
    <text>minimum</text>
  </case>
  <else><text>none</text></else>
</conditionalContent>
<conditionalContent name="cp3_characterization">
  <case condition="$fun_prime_a3 > 0 and $fun_prime_a4 &lt; 0">
    <text>maximum</text>
  </case>
  <case condition="$fun_prime_a3 &lt; 0 and $fun_prime_a4 > 0">
    <text>minimum</text>
  </case>
  <else><text>none</text></else>
</conditionalContent>
<math name="extrema_locations">$critical_points </math>
<textList name="extrema_characterizations">$cp1_characterization $cp2_characterization $cp3_characterization </textList>
<evaluate name="fun_cp1" function="$fun" input="$cp1" forceNumeric="true" displayDigits="4" />
<evaluate name="fun_cp2" function="$fun" input="$cp2" forceNumeric="true" displayDigits="4" />
<evaluate name="fun_cp3" function="$fun" input="$cp3" forceNumeric="true" displayDigits="4" />
<math name="extrema_values">$fun_cp1, $fun_cp2, $fun_cp3</math>
<number name="I1">$cp1 -$dint1[1][1] </number>
<number name="I2">$cp3 +$dint1[1][2] </number>
<evaluate name="fun_I1" function="$fun" input="$I1" forceNumeric="true" displayDigits="4" />
<evaluate name="fun_I2" function="$fun" input="$I2" forceNumeric="true" displayDigits="4" />

<conditionalContent name="global_candidates">
  <case condition="$dint1[1][3]=1">
    <mathList>$fun_I1 $fun_I2 $fun_cp2 $fun_cp3</mathList>
  </case>
  <else>
    <mathList>$fun_I1 $fun_I2 $fun_cp1 $fun_cp2</mathList>
  </else>
</conditionalContent>
<max name="global_maximum_numeric" forceNumeric="true"><mathList extend="$global_candidates[1][1]" /></max>

<conditionalContent name="global_maximum">
  <case condition="$fun_I1=$global_maximum_numeric">$fun_I1$I1</case>
  <case condition="$fun_I2=$global_maximum_numeric">$fun_I2$I2</case>
  <case condition="$dint1[1][3] != 1 and $fun_cp1=$global_maximum_numeric">$fun_cp1$cp1</case>
  <case condition="$fun_cp2=$global_maximum_numeric">$fun_cp2$cp2</case>
  <case condition="$dint1[1][3] != 3 and $fun_cp3=$global_maximum_numeric">$fun_cp3$cp3</case>
</conditionalContent>

<min name="global_minimum_numeric" forceNumeric="true"><mathList extend="$global_candidates[1][1]" /></min>
<conditionalContent name="global_minimum">
  <case condition="$fun_I1=$global_minimum_numeric">$fun_I1$I1</case>
  <case condition="$fun_I2=$global_minimum_numeric">$fun_I2$I2</case>
  <case condition="$dint1[1][3] != 1 and $fun_cp1=$global_minimum_numeric">$fun_cp1$cp1</case>
  <case condition="$fun_cp2=$global_minimum_numeric">$fun_cp2$cp2</case>
  <case condition="$dint1[1][3] != 3 and $fun_cp3=$global_minimum_numeric">$fun_cp3$cp3</case>
</conditionalContent>


</setup>


<p>Let <m>f(x) =<math extend="$fun.formula" /></m>. (Note that <m>f</m> is defined for all <m>x</m> since <m><math extend="$quartic.formula" /></m> is always positive.)</p>




<exercise>
<p>Calculate <m>f'(x)</m>.</p>

<p><m>f'(x) =</m> 
<answer>
<award>$fun_prime </award>
</answer>
</p>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<p>Find the critical points of <m>f</m>. </p>

<p>Critical points = 
<answer>
<award matchPartial="true" unorderedCompare="true">$critical_points </award>
</answer>
  (If there are multiple answers, separate by commas; do not round.)</p>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<p>Find the local extrema of <m>f</m>.  (Extrema just means either a maximum or a minimum.)  For each extremum calculate three things: the location of the extremum (i.e., value of <m>x</m>), the value of the extremum (i.e., value of <m>f(x)</m>), and whether it is a local maximum or a local minimum.</p>

<p>Locations of the local extrema: 
<answer>
<award matchPartial="true">$extrema_locations </award>
<award credit="0.8" name="award6" matchPartial="true" unorderedCompare="true">$extrema_locations </award>
</answer>
 (If multiple answers, enter in increasing order, separated by commas; if no answers, enter <alert>none</alert>.)</p>
<feedback condition="$award6">Enter in increasing order.</feedback>

<p>Values of the local extrema: 
<answer>
<award matchPartial="true" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001">$extrema_values </award>
</answer>
 (If multiple answers, enter in the same order as above, separated by commas; if no answers, enter <alert>none</alert>.  If rounding, keep at least four digits.)</p>

<p>For each extremum, enter either <alert>maximum</alert> or <alert>minimum</alert> to indicate if the extremum is a local maximum or local minimum, respectively.  (If multiple answers, enter in the same order as above, separated by commas; if no answers, enter <alert>none</alert>.)</p>

<p>Characterization of extrema= 
<answer type="text">
  <textInput name="tiExt" width="200" />
<award>
  <when><split splitBy="comma">$tiExt</split> = $extrema_characterizations</when>
</award>
</answer>
</p>



<hint>
For example, imagine that there were local extrema at <m>x=-4</m>, <m>x=-1</m>, and <m>x=3</m>.  Imagine moreover, that <m>f(-4)=0</m>, <m>f(-1)=-3</m>, and <m>f(3)=4</m>, and that these extrema were a local maximum, a local minimum, and a local maximum, respectively.  Then, the correct answer would be to enter <c>-4,-1, 3</c> in the locations blank, enter <c>0, -3, 4</c> in the values blank, and <c>maximum, minimum, maximum</c> in the characterization blank.
</hint>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<p>Find the global maximum and global minimum of the function <m>f(x)</m> on the interval <m>$I1  \le x \le $I2 </m>.</p>

<p>Global maximum: 
<answer>
<award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001">$global_maximum[1][1] </award>
</answer>
 ( If rounding, keep at least four digits.)</p>

<p>Global minimum: 
<answer>
<award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001">$global_minimum[1][1] </award>
</answer>
 ( If rounding, keep at least four digits.)</p>
</exercise>




<solution>

<setup>
<math name="fourad_abs" simplify="full">abs(4*$a *$d )</math>
<math name="b_squared" simplify="full">$b ^2</math>
</setup>

<exercise>
<m>f'(x) = <math extend="$fun_prime.formula" /></m>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<p>Since <m><math extend="$quartic.formula" /> > 0</m> for all <m>x</m>, the derivative always exists, and the critical points are where <m>f'(x)=0</m>.</p>

<p>To solve <me><math extend="$fun_prime.formula" />=0,</me>
we need the numerator to be zero.  We can factor the numerator by pulling out a <m>$fourad_abs x</m>, so that the condition for a critical point is
<me>$fourad_abs x(x^2-$b_squared ) = 0.</me>
The condition means that either <m>x=0</m> or <m>x^2 = $b_squared </m>.  The solutions are the three critical points <m>x=$cp1 </m>, <m>x=$cp2 </m>, and <m>x=$cp3 </m>.</p>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<p>The candidates for the local extrema are the critical points <m>x=$cp1 </m>, <m>x=$cp2 </m>, and <m>x=$cp3 </m>.  To determine if the critical points are local extrema, we check to see if <m>f</m> switches from increasing to decreasing or vice versa at the critical point.</p>

<p>Since <m>f'(x)</m> cannot change sign away from the critical points, i.e., in the intervals <m>(-\infty, $cp1 )</m>, <m>($cp1 ,$cp2 )</m>, <m>($cp2 ,$cp3 )</m>,  or <m>($cp3 ,\infty)</m>, we check the sign of <m>f'(x)</m> in each of those intervals.</p>

<p>To test the sign of <m>f'(x)</m> in the interval <m>(-\infty,$cp1 )</m>, we could pick the point <m>x=$auxpoint1 </m>.  <m>f'($auxpoint1 ) = $fun_prime_a1  
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a1 > 0">
\gt 
</case>
<else>
\lt 
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 0</m>.  <m>f(x)</m> is 
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a1 > 0">
increasing
</case>
<else>
decreasing
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 on the interval <m>(-\infty,$cp1 )</m>.</p>

<p>To test the sign of <m>f'(x)</m> in the interval <m>($cp1 ,$cp2 )</m>, we could pick the point <m>x=$auxpoint2 </m>.  <m>f'($auxpoint2 ) = $fun_prime_a2  
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a2 > 0">
\gt 
</case>
<else>
\lt 
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 0</m>.  <m>f(x)</m> is 
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a2 > 0">
increasing
</case>
<else>
decreasing
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 on the interval <m>($cp1 ,$cp2 )</m>.</p>

<p>To test the sign of <m>f'(x)</m> in the interval <m>($cp2 ,$cp3 )</m>, we could pick the point <m>x=$auxpoint3 </m>.  <m>f'($auxpoint3 ) = $fun_prime_a3  
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a3 > 0">
\gt 
</case>
<else>
\lt 
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 0</m>.  <m>f(x)</m> is 
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a3 > 0">
increasing
</case>
<else>
decreasing
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 on the interval <m>($cp2 ,$cp3 )</m>.</p>

<p>To test the sign of <m>f'(x)</m> in the interval <m>($cp3 ,\infty)</m>, we could pick the point <m>x=$auxpoint4 </m>.  <m>f'($auxpoint4 ) = $fun_prime_a4  
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a4 > 0">
\gt 
</case>
<else>
\lt 
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 0</m>.  <m>f(x)</m> is 
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a4 > 0">
increasing
</case>
<else>
decreasing
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 on the interval <m>($cp3 ,\infty)</m>.</p>

<p>Since <m>f(x)</m> is 
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a1 > 0">
increasing
</case>
<else>
decreasing
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 on the interval <m>(-\infty,$cp1 )</m> and <m>f(x)</m> is 
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a2 > 0">
increasing
</case>
<else>
decreasing
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 on the interval <m>($cp1 ,$cp2 )</m>, the sign of <m>f'(x)</m> does indeed change at the critical point <m>x=$cp1 .</m>  <m>f</m> has a local $cp1_characterization  at the point <m>x=$cp1 </m>.  The value of the $cp1_characterization  is <m>f($cp1 ) \approx $fun_cp1</m>.</p>

<p>Since <m>f(x)</m> is 
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a2 > 0">
increasing
</case>
<else>
decreasing
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 on the interval <m>($cp1 ,$cp2 )</m> and <m>f(x)</m> is 
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a3 > 0">
increasing
</case>
<else>
decreasing
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 on the interval <m>($cp2 ,$cp3 )</m>, the sign of <m>f'(x)</m> does indeed change at the critical point <m>x=$cp2 .</m>  <m>f</m> has a local $cp2_characterization  at the point <m>x=$cp2 </m>.  The value of the $cp2_characterization  is <m>f($cp2 ) \approx $fun_cp2</m>.</p>

<p>Since <m>f(x)</m> is 
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a3 > 0">
increasing
</case>
<else>
decreasing
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 on the interval <m>($cp2 ,$cp3 )</m> and <m>f(x)</m> is 
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$fun_prime_a4 > 0">
increasing
</case>
<else>
decreasing
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 on the interval <m>($cp3 ,\infty)</m>, the sign of <m>f'(x)</m> does indeed change at the critical point <m>x=$cp3 .</m>  <m>f</m> has a local $cp3_characterization  at the point <m>x=$cp3 </m>.  The value of the $cp3_characterization  is <m>f($cp3 ) \approx $fun_cp3</m>.</p>

<p>In summary, the locations of the extrema are: <m>$cp1 </m>, <m>$cp2 </m>, <m>$cp3 </m>.  The values of the extrema are: <m>$fun_cp1 </m>, <m>$fun_cp2 </m>, <m>$fun_cp3 </m>.  The characterization of the extrema are: $cp1_characterization , $cp2_characterization , $cp3_characterization .</p>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<p>The global extrema must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.  Therefore, the possibilities for global extremum locations are <m>x=$I1 </m>, 
<conditionalContent condition="$dint1[1][3] != 1">
  <m>x=$cp1 </m>,
</conditionalContent>
 <m>x=$cp2 </m>,
<conditionalContent condition="$dint1[1][3] != 3">
  <m>x=$cp3 </m>,
</conditionalContent>
 and <m>x=$I2 </m>.  We plug those values into <m>f</m> to determine which location gives the largest and smallest value.</p>
<md>
  <mrow>f($I1 )\amp \approx $fun_I1</mrow>
  <conditionalContent condition="$dint1[1][3] != 1">
    <mrow>f($cp1 )\amp \approx $fun_cp1</mrow>
  </conditionalContent>
  <mrow>f($cp2 )\amp \approx $fun_cp2</mrow>
  <conditionalContent condition="$dint1[1][3] != 3">
    <mrow>f($cp3 )\amp \approx $fun_cp3</mrow>
  </conditionalContent>
  <mrow>f($I2 )\amp \approx $fun_I2</mrow>
</md>

<p>The global maximum is <m>f($global_maximum[1][2] ) \approx $global_maximum[1][1]</m>.</p>

<p>The global minimum is <m>f($global_minimum[1][2] ) \approx $global_minimum[1][1]</m>.</p>
</exercise>

</solution>


</problem>